      "standardized_narrative": "At 1 January 2017 gross claims outstanding were GBP 399.227m. The year saw significant catastrophe activity in the second half (Hurricanes Harvey, Irma, Maria, Mexico Earthquake and California Wildfires) which materially impacted the Syndicate's loss ratio and increased claims outstanding and IBNR; the managing agent reports net unfavourable development on prior accident year losses (net GBP 25.7m). Reinsurers' share of claims outstanding also increased markedly due to recoveries from the catastrophe losses and quota-share reinsurance arrangements. Overall the report describes adverse prior year development driven by catastrophe losses and related reserve increases, particularly in property-related lines, with additional impacts from casualty quota-share IBNR increases and reinsurance recovery volatility.",
